# From "Intro Focus 23" (Wave VII - Voyager, CD1-2): a fuller account of F23
# than briefing-f23.gws's few lines from the F27 tape -- an actual exercise
# in observing those recently detached from physical life, gated the same
# way the source gates it: observe only, for now.

@segment  focus-23-observation
@title    Focus 23 — Observing the Newly Arrived
@levels   F23
@duration ~3m30s

say You're in Focus 23 -- the transitional reality of those who've detached from physical life.
pause 6
say You remain calm and strong, because you're still in control of yourself, and you're still bound to physical life. You can return completely, at any point you choose.
pause 8
say Observe. Perceive those who've made the transition but don't yet recognize it.
pause 8
say Perceive those who realize something has changed, but keep trying to stay in physical life anyway.
pause 8
say Perceive those who are bewildered and lost -- because they don't understand the meaning of the change. Frightened. Angry. Not knowing what to be, or what to do.
pause 10
say Perceive those who've become isolated, immobile. Locked, shocked, unable to release -- drifting, waiting.
pause 8
say Observe all of this. Here is where the many can be helped.
pause 6
say For now, become familiar. Only perceive and observe -- you're under full control of yourself, so that you can come back here when you're ready to help.
pause 8
